{%- doc -%}
  The product's own FAQs, with FAQPage structured data beside them.

  Same contract as blocks/product-brew-guide.liquid and blocks/product-origin-story.liquid: built
  for a product tab, where #236's pruning removes a tab whose panel renders nothing. The block
  emits no markup at all unless the product references at least one answerable FAQ, so the tab
  appears exactly on the products that have one.

  Consequently the CSS lives in {% stylesheet %} and NOT in an inline <style>. The pruning test is
  `panel.textContent.trim() === ''`, and a <style> element's text counts towards that, so an inline
  sheet would keep every empty panel alive and put the tab on all 42 products with no FAQs. The
  open/close icon is drawn with ::before/::after for the same reason the markup carries no <svg>:
  `svg` is on the pruning whitelist, and one would keep an otherwise-empty panel alive.

  The structured data is the point of the block, not a decoration. These answers are the only place
  on the site that says, in prose a machine can lift, what a coffee tastes like with milk or which
  grinder suits it -- so they are emitted as schema.org FAQPage for search, for answer engines and
  for the LLM crawlers that read JSON-LD in preference to prose. It sits inside the same `if` as
  the markup: structured data describing questions the page does not show is a markup violation,
  and emitting it unconditionally would also defeat the pruning above.

  Hidden behind a tab is fine. Google's own guidance allows FAQ content in expandable sections, and
  the answers are reachable by keyboard and by search-in-page once the tab is open.

  This replaces the disabled `faqs` section in templates/product.json, which rendered the same
  accordion from an inline <style> and emitted no structured data.

  Shapes, see reference_shopify_json_string_metafield_no_value:
    - custom.accordion       list.metaobject_reference -> .value is the array of metaobjects
    - accordion.title        single_line_text_field    -> plain string
    - accordion.description  rich_text_field           -> | metafield_tag, no bare drop

  A reference whose metaobject was deleted comes back nil, and an entry can be saved with a title
  and no answer, so every row is checked for both before it is drawn or described.

  Coverage on 2026-10-20: 18 of 60 active products reference at least one FAQ.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign faqs = closest.product.metafields.custom.accordion.value
  assign described = 0
-%}

{%- capture faq_items -%}
  {%- for faq in faqs -%}
    {%- assign question = faq.title | strip -%}
    {%- capture answer -%}{{ faq.description | metafield_tag }}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign answer_text = answer | strip_html | strip -%}
    {%- if question != blank and answer_text != blank -%}
      <details class="product-faqs__item">
        <summary class="product-faqs__question">
          <span>{{ question | escape }}</span>
          <span class="product-faqs__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="product-faqs__answer rte">{{ answer }}</div>
      </details>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture faq_questions -%}
  {%- for faq in faqs -%}
    {%- assign question = faq.title | strip -%}
    {%- capture answer -%}{{ faq.description | metafield_tag }}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign answer_text = answer | strip_html | strip -%}
    {%- if question != blank and answer_text != blank -%}
      {%- if described > 0 -%},{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign described = described | plus: 1 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The answer goes in as HTML, not as stripped text. Google's FAQPage spec allows
        <p> <br> <ol> <ul> <li> <a> <b> <strong> <i> <em> inside acceptedAnswer.text, and
        stripping them costs two things: strip_html removes tags but NOT entities, so
        `Ona & Co's "house" blend` would reach the structured data as the literal
        `Ona &amp; Co&#39;s &quot;house&quot; blend` with no Liquid filter able to undo it;
        and it joins paragraphs without a separator, turning two sentences into
        "...in the grinder.We recommend...". answer_text stays, as the emptiness test only.

        `| replace: '</', '<\/'` is defense-in-depth, not a required fix on this platform: Shopify's
        `json` filter already escapes `<` as the Unicode escape `\u003c` before this runs, so no
        literal `<` ever reaches the output -- a question or answer containing `</script>` cannot
        end the script element early on its own. Verified against the live storefront response, not
        assumed from the filter's docs (Codex raised this as a possible gap on PR #272; it wasn't
        one, once checked). The replace matches nothing, ever, on this platform, and stays anyway:
        it's harmless, documents the intent, and a `json` filter that does NOT escape `<` on some
        other platform would need exactly this -- so don't drop it if this idiom is ever ported.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign question_json = question | json | replace: '</', '<\/' -%}
      {%- assign answer_json = answer | strip | json | replace: '</', '<\/' -%}
      {"@type":"Question","name":{{ question_json }},"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":{{ answer_json }}}}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Tested on the captured markup rather than on a counter. `assign` inside `capture` does carry
  out, but one test against the thing actually being rendered cannot drift from it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if faq_items != blank -%}
  <div class="product-faqs">
    {%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h3 class="product-faqs__heading">{{ block.settings.heading }}</h3>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="product-faqs__list">{{ faq_items }}</div>
  </div>

  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{{ faq_questions | strip }}]}
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .product-faqs {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--gap-lg);
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .product-faqs__heading {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-h5--size);
  }

  /*
   * currentColor throughout. The panel paints itself from the product's own
   * pdp_background_color and sets the foreground to match, so a hard-coded rule would be invisible
   * on at least one of the eleven product colours.
   */
  .product-faqs__list {
    border-block-start: 1px solid currentColor;
  }

  .product-faqs__item {
    border-block-end: 1px solid currentColor;
  }

  .product-faqs__question {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--gap-md);
    padding-block: var(--gap-md);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: var(--font-paragraph--size);
    font-weight: 600;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .product-faqs__question::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  /*
   * A plus drawn in CSS rather than an <svg>, on purpose: `svg` is on the pruning whitelist in
   * sections/product-tabs.liquid, so an icon would stop an empty panel from ever being removed.
   */
  .product-faqs__icon {
    position: relative;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
  }

  .product-faqs__icon::before,
  .product-faqs__icon::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    background: currentColor;
  }

  .product-faqs__icon::before {
    top: 6px;
    left: 0;
    width: 14px;
    height: 2px;
  }

  .product-faqs__icon::after {
    top: 0;
    left: 6px;
    width: 2px;
    height: 14px;
  }

  .product-faqs__item[open] .product-faqs__icon::after {
    opacity: 0;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .product-faqs__icon::after {
      transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
    }
  }

  .product-faqs__answer {
    padding-block-end: var(--gap-md);
    font-size: var(--font-paragraph--size);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .product-faqs__answer > :first-child {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  .product-faqs__answer > :last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product FAQs",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Optional. The tab already labels the panel, so this is usually left empty."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Product FAQs"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}

